WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.635
-Our next guest
is a talented actress

00:00:02.635 --> 00:00:04.437
you know from shows such as
"Mad Men" and "WandaVision,"

00:00:04.437 --> 00:00:06.306
and the film
"If Beale Street Could Talk."

00:00:06.306 --> 00:00:08.574
She stars in the
highly-anticipated "Candyman,"

00:00:08.574 --> 00:00:10.209
which is in theaters everywhere
this Friday.

00:00:10.209 --> 00:00:11.244
Let's take a look.

00:00:12.678 --> 00:00:14.981
-Candyman isn't real.
-I saw him!

00:00:14.981 --> 00:00:19.385
-Candyman isn't real, Anthony!

00:00:19.385 --> 00:00:22.021
You know -- you know is real?

00:00:22.021 --> 00:00:23.756
Me, Anthony. Me!

00:00:23.756 --> 00:00:27.426
This. This is real.

00:00:27.426 --> 00:00:28.828
-You don't understand.

00:00:28.828 --> 00:00:30.263
-You...
-Okay, babe.

00:00:30.263 --> 00:00:33.900
I will show you that -- okay.

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:35.601
Candyman.
-No!

00:00:35.601 --> 00:00:38.805
-Candyman!
[ Glass shatters ]

00:00:38.805 --> 00:00:40.407
[ Screams ]

00:00:41.774 --> 00:00:44.243
-Don't say his name.

00:00:44.243 --> 00:00:46.312
-Don't follow me.

00:00:46.312 --> 00:00:48.380
-Please welcome to the show,
Teyonah Parris.

00:00:48.380 --> 00:00:49.815
How are you, Teyonah?

00:00:49.815 --> 00:00:51.917
-Hi, how are you?

00:00:51.917 --> 00:00:53.820
-I'm good. It's so funny.

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:56.789
I know that the original
"Candyman" came out in 1992,

00:00:56.789 --> 00:00:58.057
and yet even in the clip,

00:00:58.057 --> 00:00:59.992
when you start saying "Candyman"
in the mirror,

00:00:59.992 --> 00:01:00.927
I'm terrified.

00:01:00.927 --> 00:01:01.995
-You're terrified.

00:01:01.995 --> 00:01:05.598
I only said it on set
when I had to.

00:01:05.598 --> 00:01:07.867
I'm not messing around
with that any other times.

00:01:07.867 --> 00:01:10.236
Nah. Nah, I'm not testing fate.

00:01:10.236 --> 00:01:12.838
-No, it's one of those movies,
you just know about it, right?

00:01:12.838 --> 00:01:14.007
It's like, a thing,

00:01:14.007 --> 00:01:15.441
even for people who
hadn't seen the movie,

00:01:15.441 --> 00:01:17.376
I feel like it was just
in the culture.

00:01:17.376 --> 00:01:19.678
-Oh, my gosh.
It was most definitely.

00:01:19.678 --> 00:01:21.314
I had not seen the movie,

00:01:21.314 --> 00:01:24.617
but it was a thing that just
sort of permeated the culture,

00:01:24.617 --> 00:01:29.322
the community, and it became
a game of sorts, I guess.

00:01:29.322 --> 00:01:32.292
I mean really,
you're summoning spirits here,

00:01:32.292 --> 00:01:35.394
but you know, I guess
we could say it was a game

00:01:35.394 --> 00:01:37.630
But you know,
me and my brothers,

00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:40.733
we would go in the bathroom
and start to say it

00:01:40.733 --> 00:01:42.501
but then chicken out, like,
"Nah, nah, nah, nah."

00:01:42.501 --> 00:01:43.703
And then you just
start fighting,

00:01:43.703 --> 00:01:45.304
trying to get out of
the bathroom

00:01:45.304 --> 00:01:48.207
before somebody actually
says all five.

00:01:48.207 --> 00:01:51.010
But yeah, it just sort of
became a part of the culture

00:01:51.010 --> 00:01:52.946
and the community.

00:01:52.946 --> 00:01:55.247
-Obviously this film had a great
pedigree when it came to you.

00:01:55.247 --> 00:01:57.016
Nia DaCosta directing.

00:01:57.016 --> 00:01:58.383
Jordan Peele,
the great Jordan Peele

00:01:58.383 --> 00:01:59.585
worked on the script.

00:01:59.585 --> 00:02:01.921
And yet maybe you did
have some hesitation,

00:02:01.921 --> 00:02:03.889
because you knew exactly
how much people

00:02:03.889 --> 00:02:05.458
cared about the original?

00:02:05.458 --> 00:02:06.892
-I mean, absolutely.

00:02:06.892 --> 00:02:08.594
I care about the original,

00:02:08.594 --> 00:02:12.932
and I was like, "Look, y'all,
we can't mess this up."

00:02:12.932 --> 00:02:16.135
I want to be a part of
working with Jordan

00:02:16.135 --> 00:02:17.136
and working with Nia.

00:02:17.136 --> 00:02:18.904
I had seen Nia's "Little Woods"

00:02:18.904 --> 00:02:20.506
and I loved that she used,

00:02:20.506 --> 00:02:23.076
like how she spoke about
real-life issues

00:02:23.076 --> 00:02:26.278
like healthcare and poverty,
and so I knew,

00:02:26.278 --> 00:02:28.981
and even with Jordan,
I knew it would be elevated

00:02:28.981 --> 00:02:30.316
and it would have
something to say,

00:02:30.316 --> 00:02:33.819
so that definitely made me
want to work with them.

00:02:33.819 --> 00:02:36.022
But at the same time,
I was like,

00:02:36.022 --> 00:02:37.656
"Look, y'all,
we can't mess this up."

00:02:37.656 --> 00:02:40.893
And I think that we did
a great service

00:02:40.893 --> 00:02:42.395
to continuing the legacy,

00:02:42.395 --> 00:02:45.264
and I'm so, so proud of
being a part of it

00:02:45.264 --> 00:02:46.765
and excited for you guys
to see it.

00:02:46.765 --> 00:02:48.768
-I think one of the really
exciting things now

00:02:48.768 --> 00:02:51.738
is that we can actually see it,
in some places, certainly,

00:02:51.738 --> 00:02:54.340
with audiences, in theaters.

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:57.109
This is the kind of movie that
you want to see with people.

00:02:57.109 --> 00:02:58.144
-I know.

00:02:58.144 --> 00:03:00.380
It's been such a long wait,

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:03.349
so I'm excited that the fans
have stuck it out

00:03:03.349 --> 00:03:04.817
and waited for us.

00:03:04.817 --> 00:03:08.888
And even myself, I just went
back to the movie theaters.

00:03:08.888 --> 00:03:11.223
"Black Widow" brought me
back to the theaters.

00:03:11.223 --> 00:03:12.591
I was like, "I got to see this
in the theaters,"

00:03:12.591 --> 00:03:16.328
so I went at a matinee,
no one there, with my mask,

00:03:16.328 --> 00:03:17.764
like, "I'm gonna watch."

00:03:17.764 --> 00:03:20.700
And I loved it.
I've missed the movies so much.

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:26.039
I'm excited that people get to
experience this horror film

00:03:26.039 --> 00:03:28.674
as a collective experience.

00:03:28.674 --> 00:03:30.042
Like, it's a horror film.

00:03:30.042 --> 00:03:32.545
Sometimes you're not scared
but the person next to you

00:03:32.545 --> 00:03:34.847
is freaking out,
so you become scared, you know?

00:03:34.847 --> 00:03:36.649
You have to
experience that together.

00:03:36.649 --> 00:03:37.683
-Yes.

00:03:37.683 --> 00:03:40.019
And there is
the comedy of scares,

00:03:40.019 --> 00:03:41.720
which is one of the things
I've always loved

00:03:41.720 --> 00:03:44.090
about horror movies,
is everybody gasping

00:03:44.090 --> 00:03:45.291
and then everybody laughing

00:03:45.291 --> 00:03:46.725
because they realized
that they've been had.

00:03:46.725 --> 00:03:48.460
It's really joyous.

00:03:48.460 --> 00:03:50.363
-I'm excited. I'm excited.

00:03:50.363 --> 00:03:53.065
I'm like, it's finally here

00:03:53.065 --> 00:03:54.700
and we're going to give it
to the people.

00:03:54.700 --> 00:03:56.769
-And I know you're
in London right now.

00:03:56.769 --> 00:04:00.039
You're filming Marvel's
Captain Marvel sequel.

00:04:00.039 --> 00:04:01.073
And this is so cool.

00:04:01.073 --> 00:04:02.909
We heard you're going to
violate your NDA

00:04:02.909 --> 00:04:04.843
and tell us three things
about it.

00:04:04.843 --> 00:04:08.748
-I will tell you that
I am London.

00:04:08.748 --> 00:04:13.085
I am having an amazing time
filming the Marvels.

00:04:13.085 --> 00:04:16.089
And it's going to be
pretty epic.

00:04:16.089 --> 00:04:17.756
It's really exciting.
I can't wait.

00:04:17.756 --> 00:04:20.425
-I imagine it must have been
so exciting to be a part of,

00:04:20.425 --> 00:04:22.161
for my money, one of
the best show of the last year,

00:04:22.161 --> 00:04:23.395
"WandaVision."

00:04:23.395 --> 00:04:24.396
Here you are.

00:04:24.396 --> 00:04:25.864
How has your experience --

00:04:25.864 --> 00:04:27.667
I mean,
I guess you can talk about

00:04:27.667 --> 00:04:29.568
things that have
already happened.

00:04:29.568 --> 00:04:31.136
Was "WandaVision"
as much fun to make

00:04:31.136 --> 00:04:32.938
as it was for all of us
to watch?

00:04:32.938 --> 00:04:34.574
-Oh, my gosh.
It was such a treat.

00:04:34.574 --> 00:04:36.875
And just the people
I got to work with --

00:04:36.875 --> 00:04:39.912
I mean, Paul, Lizzie,
our creative team.

00:04:39.912 --> 00:04:43.316
Everybody was just
such a genuine human being.

00:04:43.316 --> 00:04:45.351
And then, you know,
we got stopped.

00:04:45.351 --> 00:04:47.953
We didn't finish
before the pandemic happened,

00:04:47.953 --> 00:04:49.688
and so when we came back,

00:04:49.688 --> 00:04:51.891
just really excited
to see each other

00:04:51.891 --> 00:04:55.294
and leaning on each other
in this very odd time.

00:04:55.294 --> 00:04:56.863
So, yeah, it was really special.

00:04:56.863 --> 00:04:59.932
And then to watch it after
having gone through a pandemic,

00:04:59.932 --> 00:05:01.266
even more special.

00:05:01.266 --> 00:05:03.869
It took on a whole other meaning
and a deeper level

00:05:03.869 --> 00:05:05.538
than even when we started out.

00:05:05.538 --> 00:05:06.572
-Well, it certainly showed up

00:05:06.572 --> 00:05:08.574
at a time when all of us
were desperate

00:05:08.574 --> 00:05:09.742
for something to watch,

00:05:09.742 --> 00:05:11.477
and to have it be
that quality was great.

00:05:11.477 --> 00:05:13.679
Congratulations on the movie.
-Thank you.

00:05:13.679 --> 00:05:15.881
-Continued good luck
in filming over there,

00:05:15.881 --> 00:05:17.550
and it's really nice
to meet you.

00:05:17.550 --> 00:05:20.219
-Thank you so much. Thank you.

00:05:20.219 --> 00:05:21.721
-"Candyman" is in theaters
this Friday.

